.45}]},{"s":"problem3","shows":{"p":"giant","does":"the yellow rod snaps in two and the truck veers off its line"},"state":{"text":"STUCK","w":"stick"},"do":[{"p":"rearOutline","v":"hide","w":"But"},{"p":"giant","v":"snaps","w":"snaps"},{"p":"giant","v":"veers","w":"veers"}],"shots":[{"focus":["giant.rod","giant.rl","giant.motor"],"width":0.8}]},{"s":"fix3","shows":{"p":"giant","does":"a green spring appears on the rod, the rod joins up and the rear wheels swing back straight"},"do":[{"p":"giant","v":"veersBack","w":"So"},{"p":"giant","v":"snapsBack","w":"spring"},{"p":"giant","v":"spring","w":"spring"},{"p":"giant","v":"sameBack","w":"center"}],"shots":[{"focus":["giant.rod","giant.rl","giant.motor"],"width":0.8}]},{"s":"finish","shows":{"p":"giant","does":"the headlights light up and side mirrors appear on the cab"},"do":[{"p":"giant","v":"steerBack","w":"Add"},{"p":"giant","v":"headlights","w":"headlights"},{"p":"giant","v":"mirrors","w":"mirrors","autoW":{"w0":"mirrors","o0":-0.7}}],"shots":[{"focus":["giant"],"width":0.85}]},{"s":"congrats","do":[],"shots":[{"focus":["giant"],"type":"wide"}]}],"audio":{"cards":[{"text":"10°","at":{"s":"fact","w":"10"},"d":1.4},{"text":"37 MILES","at":{"s":"fix2","w":"37"},"d":1.4}],"sfx":[{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"fix1","w":"motor"},"d":1.5},{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"how","w":"turns"},"d":1.5},{"lib":"dirt","at":{"s":"stakes","w":"clips"},"d":0.8}],"chimes":[{"s":"name"},{"s":"fact","w":"10"},{"s":"fix2","w":"37"},{"s":"congrats"}]},"codeShots":true,"why":"A long flatbed truck on an open road, seen from a little above so every wheel's angle reads: its tail swings into a post, then a motor and rod steer the rear wheels, first against the front (it pivots tight), then the same way (it tracks straight). Close high shots on the axles for each wheel change, the whole truck for each swing.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you only steer the front wheels of a long truck, you have a wide turn."},{"role":"problem","text":"But the long body cannot pivot, so its tail swings out wide toward a post."},{"role":"stakes","text":"The swinging tail clips the post and knocks it flat, and in a tight street that means a crunched bumper."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you bolt a steering motor and a rod onto the rear axle, so the back wheels can turn too."},{"role":"name","text":"This is four-wheel steering."},{"role":"how","text":"At a crawl, the motor turns the rear wheels against the front ones, and the truck pivots in a tight circle."},{"role":"fact","text":"A Mercedes S-Class turns its rear wheels up to 10 degrees and cuts its turning circle by up to about 2 meters."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But now at highway speed, rear wheels turned against the front make the tail whip around."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So above about 37 miles per hour, the rear wheels turn the same way as the front, and the truck tracks straight."},{"role":"name2","text":"Turning the same way is called in-phase steering, and the tight low-speed turn is called counter-phase."},{"role":"problem3","text":"But now if the motor fails, the rod snaps, the rear wheels stick, and the truck veers."},{"role":"fix3","text":"So you add a spring that pulls the rear wheels back to center and holds them straight."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add headlights and side mirrors, and the truck is ready for tight streets."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a truck that turns like a compact car."}]}